  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Assistance to Displaced Populations Affected by Conflict/Natural Disasters in Camp, Camp-like Settings, and Host Communities in the Central African Republic (CAR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project IOM aims to improve the living conditions of displaced populations affected by conflict/natural disasters in camp, camp-like settings, and host communities. Specifically, IOM intends to improve the living conditions of internally displaced persons (IDPs) through the distribution and set up of transitional shelter and construction of emergency latrines/family latrines, reinforce camp coordination and camp management mechanism in existing camps or camps areas, scale up data collection / information sharing on IDPs trends through the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), and improve the living conditions of IDPs through multipurpose cash grants.</narrative>
  </description>
